From 6f666f3a76d606a7a6c5de08838ed986df6e557c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elio Struyf <elio@struyfconsulting.be>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:54:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(browser): favourites as tiles, bookmarks per project,
 and panels at half width
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Favourites are icon tiles at the top of the Browser view's list. A tile opens
  its own tab, which shows in the tile (a dot while open) and not in the list.
  Its menu has Open, Rename…, Copy address, Open in browser, Go back to its
  address, Close and Remove from favourites. They replace pinned tabs in the
  Browser view: pinned Browser tabs become favourites. A session's tabs can
  still be pinned.
- ⌘D and the star save a bookmark (browser_bookmarks, migration v60): for the
  session's project or everywhere, in a folder, with Also add to favourites.
  A new tab lists favourites, the project's bookmarks, everywhere's and the
  tabs closed lately. Open bookmark… in the palette.
- Favourites and bookmarks get short names (shortTitle).
- Side, Half and Full for the browser panel, and Panels at half width in the
  rail's menu: Half shares the session area 50/50 for every right panel.
- Smoke steps "browser pin" and "browser favorites" follow the new behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RwbQ4p3tx1K7YFzxtnwACx
