 ### Added
 
+- **Favourites as tiles, bookmarks for everything else.** In the Browser view, favourites are a row of icons at the top of the list, as in Arc or Zen. A tile opens its page and keeps it, with a dot while it's open, and its menu has **Rename…**, **Go back to its address** and **Close**. Favourites take the place of pinned tabs there: pinned Browser tabs become favourites. ⌘D and the star now save a **bookmark**, shown for the session's project or **Everywhere**, in a folder if you like, with **Also add to favourites**. A new tab lists your favourites, the project's bookmarks, the ones for everywhere and the tabs closed lately. **Open bookmark…** in the palette finds any of them. Favourites and bookmarks get short names ("Seshboard | Seshboard" is "Seshboard").
+- **Panels at half width.** The browser panel's size is **Side**, **Half** or **Full**, and the rail's menu has **Panels at half width**. Half shares the session 50/50 with the conversation, for every panel on the right, and keeps doing so as the window resizes. Dragging the edge goes back to Side.
 - Group the sidebar by project: the View button picks State or Project, the order, and whether to show Done or compact rows.
 - A rail at the right edge holds a session's tools: Changes, Terminal, Browser, Preview, Ask, Agents, Commands and mods, with what's in them as badges.
 - **A browser for your sessions:** open any page, such as a pull request on GitHub, beside a session or on its own, keep several tabs, and pin the ones you want back after a restart. It is on from the start: a card in the sidebar tells about it once, and **Settings › General › Browser** turns it off. A pinned tab closes on the second middle click or ×, so one slip doesn't lose it. **Rename tab…** in a tab's menu (or a double click on it) gives it a name of your own, and a pinned tab keeps it after a restart. **Favourites** keep the sites you open often: the star in the toolbar (⌘D) adds the page, and the Browser view's sidebar, an empty tab and the empty Browser view list them, one click away. Every browser action is in the command palette too, with **Go to tab…** and **Open favourite…** to jump straight to a page. The toolbar's **⋯** menu has **Developer tools**, zoom, **Clear data for this site…** (signs you out of it) and **Clear all browsing data…**, which both ask first. Right-click in a page for its menu (open or copy a link, copy an image, spelling, Inspect). Sign-in windows (Sign in with Google and the like) open as real windows, so the sign-in finishes. A page that stops loads again by itself, a page that plays sound shows a speaker (Mute tab), zoom stays with each tab and shows in the toolbar, the mouse's back and forward buttons work in pages, a page's Copy buttons and fullscreen video work, and a page asks before it opens another app. Typing AltGr characters such as @ and { in a page on Windows and Linux works. The Browser button hides the panel and shows it again with its tabs as you left them; × in the panel closes them. **Allow browser previews** in **Settings › General › New sessions** turns off the preview of a session's dev server.
